X:16
T:Four Sisters Barn Dance
% NFF Book 2026, compiled by Ray Mulligan
C:trad
S:collected by The Bush Music Club, Sydney
N:"This dance was taught to the members of the Sydney Bush Music Club by a
N:well-known dance music ensemble. This group, known as "The Four Sisters",
N:played two button acordions, concertina and fiddle. They remembered this
N:dance as one that was popular in their youth. A very similar dance was done
N:in Nariel, where it was called "Uncle Ev's Barn Dance" after Mrs Beat
N:Klippel's Uncle Ev, from whom it had been learnt." - Bill Scott
B:Bill Scott, "Australian Folk Lore", Summit, 1976, p401
F:Four_Sisters_Barn_Dance.mp3 Four Sisters Barn Dance - played by Ingrid Wangel
R:Schottische
M:4/4
K:C
L:1/8
